    "summary": "\n<p><strong>What it shows.</strong> For a digraph \\(D\\) with out-degree at most 2, \\(D\\) has a directed Hamiltonian cycle iff the line graph of the split-and-pendant graph \\(H(D)\\) has a Hamiltonian cycle. Every vertex becomes a path <code>in – mid – out</code> with a pendant at <code>mid</code>, and every arc \\(u\\to w\\) the edge <code>out u – in w</code>. The direction DHC ⇒ EHC (<code>ehc_of_dhc</code>) is general; the converse (<code>dhc_of_ehc</code>) needs out-degree \\(\\le 2\\).</p><div class=\"ldeps\"><div><span class=\"ldeps-k\">Rests on</span><em>nothing in this figure</em></div><div><span class=\"ldeps-k\">Feeds</span><a class=\"lchip\" href=\"#cxchain-DhcTable\">DHC₂ ⟺ table<span class=\"lchip-via\">split-and-pendant</span></a></div></div>",
